# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  What to Wear — environment variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  HOW TO USE
#    1. Copy this file to `.env.local`   (cp .env.example .env.local)
#    2. Fill in the two values below.
#    3. Restart `npm run dev` — Vite only reads env files at start-up.
#
#  `.env.local` is git-ignored, so your keys never get committed.
#
#  WHERE TO FIND THEM
#    Supabase dashboard → your project → Project Settings → API
#      • "Project URL"                       → VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#      • "Project API keys" → anon / public  → VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#    (Newer projects may label the second one a "publishable" key. Use that.)
#
#  ⚠  NEVER put the `service_role` / "secret" key here. Anything starting with
#     VITE_ is bundled into the web page, so everyone can read it. The anon /
#     publishable key is designed to be public — your data is protected by the
#     row-level-security rules in supabase/schema.sql.
#
#  LEAVE BOTH BLANK to run fully offline: outfits and taste are then stored in
#  this browser only.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
